  <para style="h">Ñwed Mbon Hibru</para>
  <para style="toc1">Ñwed Mbon Hibru</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ñwed Mbon Hibru</para>
  <para style="toc3">Hbr</para>
  <para style="mt1">Ñwed Mbon Hibru</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="HEB 1" />
  <para style="s1">Krais Ado Akpatre Ikọ A-atooho Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 1:1" />Ke mme usen edem, Abasi amaatañ ikọ anọ mme ete ñnyịn ato inua mme prọfed ke uwak-uwak ini ye ke nsio-nsio usʌñ, <verse eid="HEB 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 1:2" />ado ke mme akpatre usen ami anye a-atañ ikọ inọ ñnyịn ato Ayịn amọ, a-anye amaakemek adiaakpa afịd ñkpọ, a-adooho ekenam ekondo eto ke anye. <verse eid="HEB 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 1:3" />Ayịn ado uyama ubọọñ Abasi ye ataa mbid idem amọ a-amʌmmọ afịd ñkpọ akama ke adudu ikọ amọ. Ke anye amaakenam awo asana ke adiyet idiọọkñkpọ nsio, anye amaasuuk atie ke ubọk nnasia Andikara ke hefịn. <verse eid="HEB 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 1:4" />Ndin anye amaakappa akoñ akan mme enyere sia anyịñ a-anye abọọhọ akoñ akan ake ammọ.<verse eid="HEB 1:4" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ayịn A-akpon Akan mme Enyere</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 1:5" />Sia akee ke atu mme enyere ke akenam Abasi abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:5">“Afo ado Ayịn mmi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:5">mfịn ami mmekappa ubon fiin”?</para>
  <para style="m" vid="HEB 1:5">Me adibo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:5">“Ami ñyaado Ete amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:5">ndin anye ayaado Ayịn mmi”?<verse eid="HEB 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 1:6" />Ndin ñko, ke ini Abasi abenne akpa ayịn amọ adi ederimbod, anye ate,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:6">“Yak afịd mme enyere Abasi ekpono anye.”<verse eid="HEB 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 1:7" />Ke aditañ ikọ mbaña mme enyere anye ate,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:7">“Anye anam mme enyere amọ edo sịbidịd,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:7">anyʌñ anam mbon utom amọ edo mme edeme ikañ.”<verse eid="HEB 1:7" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 1:8" />Ado ke abaña Ayịn anye abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:8">“Ebekpo mfo, O Abasi, ayaaba ke nsi-nsi, nsi-nsi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:8">esañ unen adiido esañ abioubọọñ mfo.<verse eid="HEB 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 1:9" />Afo amema adinenido, anyʌñ asua ukwañ ido;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:9">ke ntoro Abasi, Abasi mfo, u-udịppe fiin abọhọ mme</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:9">nsaña mfo ke aduyet fiin adan inemesịd.”<verse eid="HEB 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 1:10" />Anye amaana abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:10">“Ke aditọọñọ, O Abọọñ, afo akesịn itiad idakisọñ ederimbod,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:10">mme hefịn edoñño utom ubọk mfo.<verse eid="HEB 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 1:11" />Ammọ eyaetak, ado afo asʌk abaaba;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:11">ammọ eyaetaha nte afọñ.<verse eid="HEB 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 1:12" />Afo ayaafʌt ammọ nte afọñ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:12">eyaekpʌhọ ammọ nte afọñ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:12">Ado afo asʌk aba ukem-ukem</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:12">ndin mme isua mfo, tutu amama, idiinieghe utịd.”<verse eid="HEB 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 1:13" />Akenaanam akee ke atu mme enyere ke Abasi abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 1:13">“Tie ke ubọk nnasia mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:13">tutu ami nnam mme asua</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 1:13">mfo ekappa edo ifịm udodukod mfo”?<verse eid="HEB 1:13" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 1:14" />Nte mme enyere Abasi idooho mme sịbidịd nsaña utom e-esioho edọñ adinam ñkpọ nnọọ mbon e-ediibọ adinyaaña?<verse eid="HEB 1:14" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="HEB 2" />
  <para style="s1">Ñkpañutọñ A-abañake Adinyaaña</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 2:1" />Ke ntoro, ana ñnyịn itʌm ikpañ utọñ inọ se ñnyịn ikop mbaak ñnyịn idiyooñ ikpọñ usʌñ. <verse eid="HEB 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 2:2" />Sia, adieke etob a-mme enyere eketañña akebọppọ mme awo, ndin ubiaat etob ami ye ntịdutọñ edat ufen a-akedotto esọk mme awo, <verse eid="HEB 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 2:3" />die ke ñnyịn idiibọkkọ adieke ñnyịn isịnne utọ ekamba adinyaaña ami? Adinyaaña ami ado se Abọọñ ke idem amọ akebem iso asian, ndin mbon e-ekekoppo enyʌñ esọọñọ inọ ñnyịn. <verse eid="HEB 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 2:4" />Abasi amaanyʌñ anọ ikọ ntiense abaña ñkpọ ami ke mme idiọọñọ, mme utịppeñkpọ, mme utom adudu ye mme enọ Adisana Sịbidịd e-ekedeemeke nte asañake akekem ke udọñ amọ.<verse eid="HEB 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enam Yisọs Ado Ayọhọ Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 2:5" />Idooho mme enyere ke anye ayaak ederimbod a-adiidi anọ, a-ñnyịn itañña ibaña. <verse eid="HEB 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 2:6" />A-aba itie a-awo abooho:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 2:6">“Nsoo ido ubonawo a-afo akereke ñkpọ abaña anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 2:6">ayịn awo a-afo aseeghe ñkpọ abaña anye?<verse eid="HEB 2:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 2:7" />Afo akenam ammọ esuuhọ etək-etək ekan mme enyere;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 2:7">amaayat ammọ anyanya ubọọñ ye ukpono,<verse eid="HEB 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 2:8" />anyʌñ asịn afịd ñkpọ ke idak ñkpad ammọ.”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="HEB 2:8">Ke adisịn afịd ñkpọ ke idak ammọ, ibaaha ñkpọ se Abasi miikiyaaha isịn ke idak ammọ. Kpayeado idahami ñnyịn ikịtte afịd ñkpọ e-esịneke ke idak ammọ. <verse eid="HEB 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 2:9" />Ado ñnyịn imikịt Yisọs, e-ekenamma asuuhọ etək-etək akan mme enyere. Idahami, e-eyat anye anyanya ubọọñ ye ukpono sia anye amaabọ ndutʌhọ ñkpa nọ ato do, ke mfọn Abasi, anye akpa ñkpa ke iwuood afịd awo.<verse eid="HEB 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 2:10" />Ke adikoono uwak nditọ ideen ye ibaan ndʌk ubọọñ, amaadot Abasi, a-adooho ke anye, anyʌñ ato ke anye afịd ñkpọ aba, adinam andisiak usʌñ adinyaaña ukpọñ afọn ama ato ke ndutʌhọ a-anye akebọọhọ. <verse eid="HEB 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 2:11" />Ammọ naña iba, anye a-anamma awo asana ye mbon se enam esaana, esịne ke ubon keed. Ke ntoro, abuud imʌmmọ Yisọs adikoot ammọ nditọeka.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek adelfọi a-awuọñọke </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ideen ye ibaan</char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ asʌk ada anọ ideen ye ibaan e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ ke atu ubon Abasi; ñko se ke Hibru 2:12; ye ke Hibru 3:1, 12; Hibru 10:19; Hibru 13:22</char></note> <verse eid="HEB 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 2:12" />Anye ate,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 2:12">“Ami ñyaayaara anyịñ mfo nnọ mme nditọeka mmi ideen ye ibaan;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 2:12">ami ñyaakwọ itooro mfo ke atu esob mbon Abasi.”<verse eid="HEB 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 2:13" />Mfen ñko,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 2:13">“Ami ñyaabuọt idem mmi ye anye.”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="HEB 2:13">Anye amaana abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 2:13">“Se ami mi, ye nditọ A-Abasi annọọhọ miin.”<verse eid="HEB 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 2:14" />Sia nditọ e-enie abʌk ye iyiib, anye ñko amaawana ke uduud awo, nọ ato ke ñkpa amọ anye abiat anye a-akamake adudu ñkpa, a-adooho, andidiọọk, <verse eid="HEB 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 2:15" />ndin anyʌñ atat mbon a-ndịk ñkpa akesịnne ifʌn ke afịd ayio uwem ammọ. <verse eid="HEB 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 2:16" />Sia ke akpanikọ idooho mme enyere ke anye anyaaña, ado ado ubon Ebraham. <verse eid="HEB 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 2:17" />Ke ntak ami akena enam anye aba nte ammọ, nte awo ke afịd usʌñ, nọ ato do anye akappa ado ekamba aku Abasi a-anieghe mbọm anyʌñ asọọñọ ada ke mbuọdidem ke utom Abasi, nọ ato do anye afeen mme idiọọkñkpọ awo. <verse eid="HEB 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 2:18" />Sia adooho anye ke idem amọ amaabọ ndutʌhọ ke ini ekedomoke anye, anye a-anie ukem adinyaña mbon e-ebaaha ke idomo.<verse eid="HEB 2:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="HEB 3" />
  <para style="s1">Yisọs A-akpon Akan Moses</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 3:1" />Ke ntoro, ndisana nditọeka ke Krais, ideen ye ibaan e-ewanake ke ikood, iwuuk akikere ndufo ke Yisọs, a-ñnyịn idiọọñọke nte abọsịd ye ekamba aku. <verse eid="HEB 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 3:2" />Anye amaasọọñọ ada anam akpanikọ ye anye a-akemekke anye, kpa naña Moses akesọọñọ ada anam akpanikọ ke atu afịd nditọ Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 3:3" />Emaekịt Yisọs nte anye a-adotto adibọ ukpono a-akponno akan Moses, kpa naña andibọp ufọk anie ukpono akponno akan ufọk ke idem amọ. <verse eid="HEB 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 3:4" />Sia awo ado andibọp afịd ufọk, ado Abasi ado andibọp afịd ñkpọ. <verse eid="HEB 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 3:5" />“Moses amaanam akpanikọ nte ayịnufọk ke atu afịd ufọk Abasi,” atañ ikọ ntiense abaña se ediitañ ke ini iso. <verse eid="HEB 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 3:6" />Ado Krais anam akpanikọ nte Ayịn a-aseeghe ñkpọ abaña ufọk Abasi. Ndin ñnyịn ido ufọk amọ, adieke ñnyịn imʌmmọ eti ido ñnyịn ikama ye idodanyen a-ñnyịn idatta itañ ase.<verse eid="HEB 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndʌdutọñ A-abañake Unana Mbuọdidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 3:7" />Ke ntoro, kpa naña Adisana Sịbidịd atañ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 3:7">“Mfịn ami, adieke ndufo ekoppo uyio amọ,<verse eid="HEB 3:7" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 3:8" />ikiisọñ esịd ndufo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 3:8">naña ekenam ke ini nsọñiwuod,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:8">ke ini idomo ke anaan,<verse eid="HEB 3:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 3:9" />itie a-mme eteete ndufo ekendomoke miin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:9">akpesʌkado ammọ emaekịt se ñkenam ke isua aba.<verse eid="HEB 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 3:10" />Ado akenam ami mmaayat esịd ye emana ado, ndin ami ñnyʌñ mbo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:10">‘Esịd ammọ awawakka akpọñ usʌñ afịd ini,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:10">ndin ammọ idiọọñọke usʌñ mmi.’<verse eid="HEB 3:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 3:11" />Ndin ami mmaanwọñọ ke iyadesịd mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:11">‘Ammọ idiidʌkkọ ke nduọkadudu mmi.’ ”<verse eid="HEB 3:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 3:12" />Nditọeka mmi ke Krais, ikịt ibo ke awo ndufo ndomokeed inieghe idiọọk ido ye esịd i-imiinịmme ke akpanikọ a-anyʌññọ awakka akpọñ usʌñ Abasi uwem. <verse eid="HEB 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 3:13" />Ado isọọñọ emọ-emọ idem ke usen ke usen, adaña nte ekoodo anye “Mfịn,” mbaak awo ndufo ndomokeed adikappa anie esịd itiad ato ke abiaña idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="HEB 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 3:14" />Ñnyịn imidi adiwuana ke Krais adieke ñnyịn idiikan isọñ ubọk imʌm mbuọdidem a-ñnyịn ikinieghe ke akpa ikama tutu asịm utịd. <verse eid="HEB 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 3:15" />Nte esʌkkọ ebo idahado:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 3:15">“Mfịn ami, adieke ndufo ekoppo uyio amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:15">ikiisọñ esịd naña ekenam</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 3:15">ke ini nsọñiwuod.”<verse eid="HEB 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 3:16" />Mme anie ikikop inyʌñ isọñ iwuod ado? Nte idooho mbon ake Moses akesañake keed awuọ ke isọñ Iyib? <verse eid="HEB 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 3:17" />Mfen ñko, mme anie ke anye akeyat esịd abaña ke afịd isua aba? Nte idooho ye mbon e-ekenamma idiọọkñkpọ, a-akpo ammọ aketakka ke anaan? <verse eid="HEB 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 3:18" />Ndin mme anie ke Abasi akenwọñọ abo ke ammọ idiidʌkkọ ke nduọkadudu amọ, miidooho mbon ntreutọñ i-imiikikoppo item? <verse eid="HEB 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 3:19" />Ke ntoro, ñnyịn imikịt ke ammọ ikikanna idʌk ato ke unana adinịm ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="HEB 3:19" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="HEB 4" />
  <para style="s1">Nduọkadudu Sabad Ana Anọ Ikọd Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 4:1" />Ke ntoro, sia enwọñọ adidʌk ke nduọkadudu amọ asʌkkọ ababa, yak ñnyịn ikpeme mbaak ndufo ndomokeed aditre adidʌk ke esịd. <verse eid="HEB 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 4:2" />Sia emaekwọrọ eti etob inọ ñnyịn ñko, kpa naña ekekwọrọ enọ ammọ; ado etob a-ammọ ekekoppo ikiwuọñọke ñkpọ inọ ammọ, sia ammọ ikiwuanake ke mbuọdidem mbon e-ekesuuhọ iwuod. <verse eid="HEB 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 4:3" />Idahami ñnyịn i-imaikinịm ke akpanikọ imidʌk ke nduọkadudu, ukem naña Abasi amaaketatañ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 4:3">“Ndin ke iyadesịd mmi ami mmaanwọñọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 4:3">‘Ammọ idiidʌkkọ ke nduọkadudu mmi.’ ”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="HEB 4:3">Ado utom amọ amaakweeñe tọọñọ ke ini e-ekebotto ederimbod. <verse eid="HEB 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 4:4" />Sia a-aba itie a-atañña abaña ayọhọ usen itiaba ke mme ikọ ami: “Ndin ke ayọhọ usen itiaba Abasi amaaduọk adudu ke afịd utom amọ.” <verse eid="HEB 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 4:5" />Ñko, ke se ñnyịn imaikikokoot anye a-atatañ abo: “Tutu amama ammọ idiidʌkkọ ke nduọkadudu mmi.”<verse eid="HEB 4:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 4:6" />Ke ntoro sia adooho usʌk awo idʌkkọ kaña ke nduọkadudu ado, ndin sia mbon e-eketooho ekwọrọ eti etob enọ ikidʌkkọ ke esịd, ato ke ntịdutọñ, <verse eid="HEB 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 4:7" />Abasi amaamaana asio usen anịm, akoot “Mfịn,” a-adooho ke anyan ini anye amaatañ ikọ ato inua Defid, kpa naña ewet ke itie ñwed e-emaekekokoot:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 4:7">“Mfịn ami, adieke ndufo ekoppo uyio amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 4:7">ikiisọñ esịd ndufo.”<verse eid="HEB 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 4:8" />Sia akpedo Yọsua amaanọ ammọ nduọkadudu, Abasi ikpikimaanake itañ ibaña usen mfen. <verse eid="HEB 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 4:9" />Ke ntoro, Sabad nduọkadudu a-asʌhọ anọ mbon Abasi; <verse eid="HEB 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 4:10" />sia awo akeedodo a-adʌkkọ ke nduọkadudu Abasi a-aduọk adudu ke utom ammọ, kpa naña Abasi akeduọk adudu ke utom amọ. <verse eid="HEB 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 4:11" />Ke ntoro, yak ñnyịn idomo afịd ukeme adidʌk ke nduọkadudu ado, mbaak awo ndomokeed adiduọ ke adikeene uwọdñkpọ unana ñkobitem ammọ.<verse eid="HEB 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 4:12" />Sia ikọ Abasi anie uwem anyʌñ anie adudu, asọp akan akankañ a-anieghe inua iba, anie adudu adiboiyo ndʌk esịd, tutu abakka ukpọñ ye sịbidịd, ñkikek idem ye ñkpadia akpọ. Anye akpe ikpe a-abañake akikere esịd ye edu unam ñkpọ ke esịd. <verse eid="HEB 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 4:13" />Ibaaha ñkpọ ndomokeed ke afịd se ekebot a-adịbeke ke anyen Abasi. E-efʌkkọ afịd ñkpọ enịm inwañ ke iso anye a-ñnyịn inieghe adinam ibad nnọọ.<verse eid="HEB 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Ado Akwa Aku Ñnyịn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 4:14" />Ndin, sia ñnyịn imainie Yisọs, Ayịn Abasi adooho ekamba aku a-amaakesaña aboiyo ke mme hefịn, yak ñnyịn itʌm imʌm akpanikọ ikama ke abaña mbuọdidem a-ñnyịn isọọñọke itañ ibaña. <verse eid="HEB 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 4:15" />Sia ñnyịn inieghe ekamba aku i-imiinieghe esịd mbọm ibaña mmemidem ñnyịn, ado inie anye a-adooho emaedomo anye ke afịd usʌñ naña enyʌñ idomo ñnyịn, ado anye ikinamma idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="HEB 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 4:16" />Yak ñnyịn ndin isaña uko-uko ikpere ebekpo mfọn Abasi, nọ ato do ñnyịn ibọ mbọm ye mfọn a-adiinyaaña ñnyịn ke ini nnananyen.<verse eid="HEB 4:16" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="HEB 5" />
  <para style="s1">Mfọnmma Akwa Aku</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 5:1" />Esio afịd ekamba aku ke atu mme awo, enyʌñ emek anye ebo ada ke iwuod mme awo ke mme ñkpọ a-abañake Abasi, ke adinọ mme enọ ye adinam mme uwa ke ntak mme idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="HEB 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 5:2" />Anye a-akan ayọ mbon unana ifiọk e-ewakkake ekpọñ usʌñ, sia anye ke idem amọ ado awo a-anieghe mmemidem. <verse eid="HEB 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 5:3" />Ami ado ntak a-anaaha anye anam mme uwa ke ntak mme idiọọkñkpọ amọ ye ake mbon mfen. <verse eid="HEB 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 5:4" />Ndin awo ndomokeed idatta ukpono ami inọ idem amọ, ibọhọke Abasi akoot anye naña ekekoot Erọn.<verse eid="HEB 5:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 5:5" />Kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, Krais ikinọọhọ idem amọ ubọọñ adido ekamba aku. Ado Abasi akebo anye:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 5:5">“Afo ado Ayịn mmi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 5:5">mfịn ami mmekappa ubon fiin.”<verse eid="HEB 5:5" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 5:6" />Ndin anye abo ke itie mfen ate:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 5:6">“Afo ado aku ke nsi-nsi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 5:6">ke ukem ndaha Melkisedek.”<verse eid="HEB 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 5:7" />Ke mme usen uwem Yisọs ke ederimbod, anye amaabọñ akam anyʌñ abeeñe mme ebeeñe ke akpọsọñ uyio, ye mmọọñayịd anọ anye a-akpekenyaañake anye asio ke ñkpa, ndin emaekop enọ anye ato ke nsuukidem ammọ. <verse eid="HEB 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 5:8" />Akpesʌkado a-anye akedooho Ayịn, anye amaakpeep ñkobitem ato ke mme ukuud a-akesịmme anye, <verse eid="HEB 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 5:9" />ndin ke emaekenam anye afọn ama, anye amaakappa ado usʌñ nsi-nsi adinyaaña anọ afịd mbon e-ekoppo item enọ anye. <verse eid="HEB 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 5:10" />Ndin Abasi amaamek anye nte ekamba aku ke ukem ndaha Melkisedek.<verse eid="HEB 5:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndʌdutọñ Mbaak Ediwuọ Ekpọñ Usʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 5:11" />Ñnyịn iminie uwak ñkpọ se ikpitañ ibaña ñkpọ ami, ado asọsọñ adinam nọ inwaña ndufo sia ñkpọ mmisọppọ inwaña ndufo aba. <verse eid="HEB 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 5:12" />Akpesʌkado, ke aditʌm ntañ ndufo ekpekap edo mme andikpeeb, ado idahami ado se awo amamaana atọọñọ ikpeep ndufo akpa ntọọñọ ukpeebñkpọ a-abañake ikọ Abasi. Ndufo edo se enọ mmọọñeba, idooho nsọọñ ndidia! <verse eid="HEB 5:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 5:13" />Awo akeedodo a-anwọññọ mmọọñeba nọ ato do anye adu uwem, ke ntak asʌkkọ ado nsekayịn, imegheke ye ukpeebñkpọ a-abañake adinenido. <verse eid="HEB 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 5:14" />Ado nsọọñ ndidia ana anọ mme adiọọñọidem awo, a-adooho ke adidia afịd ini, ammọ ekpeep idem ammọ adidiọọñọ ukpʌhọde eti ye idiọọk.<verse eid="HEB 5:14" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="HEB 6" />
  <para style="s1">Unọmọ Adiwuọ Ñkpọñ Usʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 6:1" />Ke ntoro yak ñnyịn ikpọñ ndin mme akpa ntọọñọ ukpeebñkpọ a-abañake Krais, nọ ato do ikpoon, inyʌñ ikọd ke ifiọk. Yak ikiimamaana isịn itiad idakisọñ adikappa esịd ñkpọñ mme ñkpọ e-edatta awo eka ñkpa, ye mbuọdidem ke Abasi, ye <verse eid="HEB 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 6:2" />ukpeebñkpọ a-abañake adinam asana, udodubọk, adised ke ñkpa ye ubiideikpe nsi-nsi. <verse eid="HEB 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 6:3" />Ndin ke Abasi anyịmmeke, iyainam ntoro.<verse eid="HEB 6:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 6:4" />Ado ataa akpọsọñ ñkpọ anọ mbon e-emaekebọ ntadanyen, e-emaeketappa mme enọ mfọn Abasi ekop, e-emaekekeene ewuana ke Adisana Sịbidịd <verse eid="HEB 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 6:5" />e-emaekekịt ufọn a-asịneke ke ikọ Abasi ye adudu emana a-adiighe ke iso, <verse eid="HEB 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 6:6" />adieke ewuọọñọke ekpọñ usʌñ, adikan mmaana nnam ammọ ekappa esịd. Sia ke ntakudua ammọ, ammọ emamaana ekọñ Ayịn Abasi ke krọọs enyʌñ enam anye abọ asuenne anwa-anwa. <verse eid="HEB 6:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 6:7" />Isọñ a-anwọññọ mmọọñ e-edịm adeppe ndin-ndin aduọkkọ, a-anyʌññọ anwịm mfịd a-afọnnọ ye mme andikitọ anye asibọbọ adidiọñ Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 6:8" />Ado isọñ a-anwịmme mme ñkukịm ye mbaraekpe ibaaha ufọn, ndin esisọsuuñọ anye enyʌñ efọp anye ke ikañ ke akpatre.<verse eid="HEB 6:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 6:9" />Ndima ufan mmi ke Krais, akpesʌkado a-ñnyịn itañña ntom, ñnyịn iminekke inịm Abasi ke akpanikọ ibaña mme nti ñkpọ e-esañake ye adinyaaña ndufo. <verse eid="HEB 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 6:10" />Abasi ado anam unen; anye idiifreke utom ye ima a-ndufo ewọttọ anye, kpa naña ndufo enyaaña ikọt ammọ enyʌñ ekaka iso enyanya ammọ. <verse eid="HEB 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 6:11" />Ñnyịn iyem afịd ndufo ewọt ukem-ukem ntịñanyen ami ke afịdesịd tutu ataa akpatre, nọ ato do se ndufo enie idodanyen ebaña atʌm awuọ ada ayọhọ-ayọhọ. <verse eid="HEB 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 6:12" />Ñnyịn iyemme ndufo edoñno ifu, ado edubọiyọ mbon a-atooho ke mbuọdidem ye ime, ammọ ebọ se Abasi amaakenwọñọ.<verse eid="HEB 6:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enwọñọ Abasi Asọsọọñọ Ada</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 6:13" />Ke ini Abasi akenamma enwọñọ anọ Ebraham, sia awo ndomokeed a-akekponno akan anye imiikibaaha se anye akpedat anwọñọ, anye amaanwọñọ ke idem amọ, <verse eid="HEB 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 6:14" />anyʌñ abo: “Ke akpanikọ ami ñyaudiọñ fiin ñnyʌñ unọ uwak nditọ e-etooho ubon mfo.” <verse eid="HEB 6:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 6:15" />Ndin ke emaekebet ke ime, Ebraham amaabọ se Abasi akenwọñọ anọ anye.<verse eid="HEB 6:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 6:16" />Mme awo esinwọñọ ke anyịñ awo se ikpon ikan ammọ, ndin enwọñọ ado asọọñọ se etañ anyʌñ atre afịd mfaaña. <verse eid="HEB 6:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 6:17" />Sia Abasi akeyem adinam uduak amọ i-imiisikpəhoke uduud anwaña mbon a-anye akenamma enwọñọ ado anọ, anye amaasọọñọ ke enwọñọ. <verse eid="HEB 6:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 6:18" />Abasi akenam ami nọ ato do, ke mme ñkpọ iba imiikemeke adikpəho, A-Abasi ñko i-imiikemeke isʌhọ nsu, ñnyịn i-imaikifeeñe idimʌm idodanyen e-enịmme inọọ ñnyịn, inie ayọhọ ndọñesịd. <verse eid="HEB 6:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 6:19" />Ñnyịn iminie idodanyen nte añkọ ukpọñ a-adaaha kwak. Anye aboiyo adʌk ataa esịd adisana itie, ke edem afọñ anyenusʌñ, <verse eid="HEB 6:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 6:20" />itie a-Yisọs, aboiyo iso ñnyịn, amaakibem ñnyịn iso adʌk ke iwuod ñnyịn. Anye a-akappa ekamba aku ke nsi-nsi kpa ke ukem ndaha Melkisedek.<verse eid="HEB 6:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="HEB 7" />
  <para style="s1">Melkisedek Akwa Aku</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 7:1" />Melkisedek ami akedo adidem Salem ye aku Abasi Andikoñ Ñkan. Anye akekịt Ebraham naña anyọñ ekọñ a-anye akekanna mme ndidem anyʌñ adiọñ anye. <verse eid="HEB 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 7:2" />Ndin Ebraham amaanọ anye ubaak keed ke itie duob afịd ñkpọ. Ke akpa ifed, Melkisedek awuọñọ “adidem adinenido,” ñko “adidem Salem” awuọñọ “adidem emem.” <verse eid="HEB 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 7:3" />Anye ikinieghe ete me eka, ikinieghe ntịppe, inieghe ntọọñọ usen me utịd uwem. Anye abit Ayịn Abasi anyʌñ ado aku ke nsi-nsi.<verse eid="HEB 7:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 7:4" />Kere baña naña anye akekpon atre, tutu ado se ete ñnyịn Ebraham anọ anye ubaak keed ke itie duob ke afịd mbịme ñkpọekọñ! <verse eid="HEB 7:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 7:5" />Idahami, ke idak mbed, ana ubon Lifai e-ekappake edo mme aku ebọ eto emọ-emọ mbon Isrel ayọhọ ubaak keed ke itie duob, akpesʌkado ammọ ñko e-edooho ubon Ebraham. <verse eid="HEB 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 7:6" />Kpayeado, awo ami ikitooho ntịppe Lifai, ado anye amaabọ Ebraham ayọhọ ubaak duob anyʌñ adiọñ anye a-akenieghe mme enwọñọ ado. <verse eid="HEB 7:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 7:7" />Ñko, eyịghe ndomokeed ibaaha, awo andisịp ñkan abọ adidiọñ ato anye a-akponno akan anye. <verse eid="HEB 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 7:8" />Ke ñkañ keed, ado mme akpañkpa ebọ ayọhọ ubaak keed ke itie duob; ado ke ñkañ mfen, anye ado aduuwem awo abọ ayọhọ mbaak keed ke itie duob. <verse eid="HEB 7:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 7:9" />Awo akeme adikpibo ke Lifai, a-abọọhọ ayọhọ mbaak duob, akpekpe ayọhọ mbaak duob ato Ebraham, <verse eid="HEB 7:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 7:10" />sia ke ini Melkisedek akesooboke ye Ebraham, Lifai mmọdo akesʌk asịne ke idem etebom amọ.<verse eid="HEB 7:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yisọs Aba nte Melkisedek</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 7:11" />Adieke ekpekekanna enie mfọnmma eto ke idak ubonoñkpọ mme aku Lifai, sia aketo ke ntak ami enọ mme awo mme mbed, ntak e-ekekịtte ufọn aku mfen adidi ke ukem ndaha Melkisedek, idooho ke ndaha ubonoñkpọ Erọn-o? <verse eid="HEB 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 7:12" />Sia ke ini ekpəhoke ukara aku, ana ekpəho mbed ñko. <verse eid="HEB 7:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 7:13" />Anye e-etañña mme ikọ ami ebaña aketo aduuk mfen, ndin kpaanaanam anamutom itie uwa itooho aduuk ado. <verse eid="HEB 7:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 7:14" />Sia afịd awo e-ediọọñọ ke ntịppe Abọọñ ñnyịn akedo ke ufọk Yuda, a-adooho Moses ikitañña ñkpọ ndomokeed ibaña ammọ adido aku. <verse eid="HEB 7:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 7:15" />Ndin se ñnyịn itañ ami a-anam anekke anwaña, adieke aku mfen nte Melkisedek awuọhọ ada, <verse eid="HEB 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 7:16" />a-akekappake ado aku, idooho ke ntak ntịppe ufọk emana awo me ewʌhọ, ado ke ntak adudu uwem a-mmiikemekekeme adisobo. <verse eid="HEB 7:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 7:17" />Sia ikọ Abasi a-asọọñọ abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 7:17">“Afo ado aku ke nsi-nsi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 7:17">ke ukem idaha Melkisedek.”<verse eid="HEB 7:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 7:18" />Emaetuut akpa ewʌhọ enịm sia anye imiikibaaha ufọn <verse eid="HEB 7:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 7:19" />(sia mbed ikikanna inam ñkpọ ndomokeed afọn ama), ndin e-eben idodanyen a-afọnnọ akan edi, a-adooho ke anye, ñnyịn itʌm isaña ikpere Abasi.<verse eid="HEB 7:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 7:20" />Ndin aketo ke unwọñọ! Mbon mfen emaedo mme aku, itooho ke unwọñọ, <verse eid="HEB 7:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 7:21" />ado anye amaakappa ado aku a-asañake ye unwọñọ ke ini Abasi akebooho anye ate:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 7:21">“Abọọñ a-anwọñọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 7:21">ndin idiikpəhoke akikere:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 7:21">Afo ado aku ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="HEB 7:21" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 7:22" />Ato ke ntak unwọñọ ami, Yisọs akappa atie ubiọñ ke ufa edioomo a-afọnnọ akan.<verse eid="HEB 7:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 7:23" />Idahami uwak utọ mme aku ado emaediba sia ñkpa ikidiyakka ammọ ekaiso edinam utom ado; <verse eid="HEB 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 7:24" />ado, sia Yisọs aduuho uwem ke nsi-nsi, utom amọ nte aku ada ke nsi-nsi. <verse eid="HEB 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 7:25" />Ke ntoro anye a-akan adinyaaña mbon e-ediighe ebịne Abasi ato ke anye ayọhọ-ayọhọ, sia anye adu uwem afịd ini adinam ñkpeubọk nnọọ ammọ.<verse eid="HEB 7:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 7:26" />Ke akpanikọ utọ akwa aku ado a-akan ayọ mme mfịna ñnyịn, sia anye asana, anana ndo, asana ama, ndin e-emaebakka anye esio ekpọñ mme anamidiọọk, edịppe anye edọọk ekpọñ mme hefịn. <verse eid="HEB 7:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 7:27" />Anye itieghe nte mme akwa aku mfen, inieghe adiwa uwa kwa usen, awa akpa abaña mme ndiọiñkpọ amọ, ndin adiwa abaña ndiọiñkpọ mbon mfen. Anye akewa uwa abaña mme ndiọiñkpọ mbon awo akañ keed kpọd, ke ini anye akeyakka idem amọ anọ nte ñkpọ uwa. <verse eid="HEB 7:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 7:28" />Sia mbed amek mbon e-enieñeke mmemidem nte mme akwa aku; ado enwọñọ a-akediighe adikịt mbed, akemek Ayịn, e-emaekenam afọn ama ke nsi-nsi.<verse eid="HEB 7:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="HEB 8" />
  <para style="s1">Akwa Aku Ufa Edioomo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 8:1" />Akpan ñkpọ a-ñnyịn itañña ibaña ado ami: Ñnyịn iminie utọ ekamba aku ado, a-akesuuhọ atie ke ubọk nnasia ebekpo Ubọọñ Andikara ke hefịn, <verse eid="HEB 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 8:2" />anyʌññọ anam utom ke adisana itie, atayad akpanikọ A-Abọọñ ke idem amọ akenịmme, idooho ñkaña awo.<verse eid="HEB 8:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 8:3" />Emek afịd akwa aku adinọ mme enọ ñnyʌñ ñwaa mme uwa. Ke ntoro akena anye ami ñko anyʌñ anie ñkpọ adinọ. <verse eid="HEB 8:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 8:4" />Adieke anye akpekebaaha ke ederimbod, anye ikpikidooho aku, sia mme aku ebaba e-enọọhọ mme enọ naña mbed atemme. <verse eid="HEB 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 8:5" />Ammọ enam utom ke adisana itie ukpono a-abitte anyʌñ ado ndukpọñ mme ñkpọ se iba ke hefịn. Ami ado ntak e-ekedʌttọ Moses utọñ idaha a-anye akebeeñeke idem adibọp atayad: “Kịt bo ke amenam afịd ñkpọ aba ukem-ukem nte se ekuwọt fiin ke anyọñ ekamba abod.” <verse eid="HEB 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 8:6" />Ado ke akpanikọ ubiọñutom a-Yisọs abọọhọ a-akpon akan ake ammọ, kpa naña edioomo a-anye adooho atie ubiọñ akoñño akan akaan edioomo, sia ufa edioomo akọñọ ke mme enwọñọ e-efọnnọ ekan.<verse eid="HEB 8:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 8:7" />Sia adieke akpedooho akpa edioomo ado ikinieghe ndo; awo ikpikiyemme edioomo mfen. <verse eid="HEB 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 8:8" />Ado Abasi amaasua anọ mme awo amaanyʌñ abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:8">“Mme usen esʌk edi, Abọọñ atañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:8">a-ami ndiinam</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:8">ufa edioomo ye mbon Isrel,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:8">ye mbon Yuda ñko.<verse eid="HEB 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 8:9" />Anyem idiibaaha nte</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:9">edioomo a-ami ñkenamma ye mme eteete</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:9">ammọ ke ini ami ñkemʌmmọ ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:9">ke ubọk ñwuọ ñkpọñ isọñ Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:9">sia ammọ ikisọọñọke ida ke ewʌhọ mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:9">ndin ami mmaawọññọ ñkpọñ ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:9">Abọọñ atañ.<verse eid="HEB 8:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 8:10" />Anye ami ado edioomo a-ami ndiinam ye mbon Isrel</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:10">ini ado amaaboiyo, Abọọñ atañ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:10">Ami ñyaasịn mme mbed mmi ke akikere ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:10">ñnyʌñ ñwet ke esịd ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:10">Ami ñyaado Abasi ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:10">ammọ eyaenyʌñ edo ikọd mmi.<verse eid="HEB 8:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 8:11" />Ammọ idiikpeebe mbọhọidʌñ ammọ aba,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:11">me emọ-emọ ibo, ‘Diọọñọ Abọọñ,’</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 8:11">sia afịd ammọ eyaendiọọñọ miin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:11">tọọñọ ke andisịb ñkan tutu akewuọ andikpon ñkan.<verse eid="HEB 8:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 8:12" />Sia ami ñyaafeen mme ibak ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 8:12">ndiinyʌññọ ntoiyo mme ndiọiñkpọ ammọ aba.”<verse eid="HEB 8:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 8:13" />Ke anye adikoot akaaña ami “ufa,” anye a-anam akpa akappa ado akaan, ndin se imaikikaana inyʌñ isọñ ayaasọp aboiyo afep.<verse eid="HEB 8:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="HEB 9" />
  <para style="s1">Ukpono Abasi ke Atayad Ederimbod</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 9:1" />Ndin akpa akaaña amaanie mme mbed ukpono anyʌñ anie adisana itie ukpono amọ ke isọñ. <verse eid="HEB 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 9:2" />Emaebọp atayad; ndin ke esịd akpa ubeed emaedaaha ñkpọ udod utuenikañ, akpokoro ye adisana uyo. Ekekoot itie ado, Adisana Itie. <verse eid="HEB 9:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 9:3" />Ke edem ayọhọ afọñ ikpeghe iba amaaba ubeed e-ekekoodo Ataa Adisana Itie, <verse eid="HEB 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 9:4" />e-ekenịmme itie uwa a-kold ukama mfọp insensi ye akebe edioomo e-ekedatta kold efʌk. Atu kold mmana, esañ Erọn a-aketịppeke emịne, ye mme itiad ñwed edioomo ekedọñọ ke akebe ado. <verse eid="HEB 9:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 9:5" />Mme serubim Ubọọñ Abasi ekedoro ke anyọñ akebe ado enyʌñ efʌk ufʌkñkpọ adifeen usio isob, ado ñnyịn idiikanna itañ ibaña afịd ñkpọ ado idahami.<verse eid="HEB 9:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 9:6" />Ke emaekebono afịd ñkpọ ema, mme aku ekesidʌk akpa ubeed ndin-ndin enam utom ammọ. <verse eid="HEB 9:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 9:7" />Ado ekamba aku ikpọọñ akesidʌk esịd ubeed, ndin akesinam ntom akañ keed kpọd ke isua. Anye ikpikikanna inam ami ibọhọke anye asaña ye iyiib, a-anye akesinọọhọ ke iwuod amọ, anyʌñ anọ ke ntak nnamndue a-mme awo ekesinamma ke unana adidiọọñọ. <verse eid="HEB 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 9:8" />Ke adinam ntom ke Adisana Sịbidịd akeben awọt abo ke awo ikiyaarake usʌñ adisaña ndʌk Nsana Mma Adisana Itie adaña nte akpa atayad akesʌkkọ ababa. <verse eid="HEB 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 9:9" />Ami ado uwọdñkpọ e-enọọhọ idahami adiwọt ke mme enọ ye mme uwa e-ekesiwaaha ikikanna iyet esịd mme andikpono Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 9:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 9:10" />Mme ñkpọ ami ebaña ndidia ye ukọd ye mme nsio-nsio ndutʌm adinam asana ke anwa, e-edooho mme ndutʌm e-ekesinamma, e-enyʌññọ eyaak aba tutu ini ufa ubonoñkpọ adikem.<verse eid="HEB 9:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Iyiib Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 9:11" />Ado ke ini Krais amaakedi nte akwa aku nti ñkpọ e-ebaahaba mi, anye amaaboiyo ke atayad a-akponno akan, anana ndo, idooho ubọkawo anam, a-awuọñọke ke idooho ñkpọ e-ekebottobot. <verse eid="HEB 9:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 9:12" />Anye ikiboiyoke idʌk ato ke iyiib ebod me ake abaakenañ; ado akekama iyiib amọ adʌk ke Nsana Mma Adisana Itie ini keed kpọd, anyʌñ abọ nsi-nsi ufak anọ afịd awo. <verse eid="HEB 9:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 9:13" />Iyiib ebod ye ñyaara enañ ye ntọñ abaak uman enañ e-ekesidatta esiime mbon i-imiisanake, amaanam ammọ esana ke ikpọkidem. <verse eid="HEB 9:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 9:14" />Die ndin ke iyiib Krais, a-akedooho ke ntak Sịbidịd nsi-nsi ke akeyaak idem amọ nte anana ndo adisana uwa anọ Abasi, imiidiiyette esịd ñnyịn isịññe mme adinam a-adatta aka ñkpa ifep, nọ ñnyịn ikan ikpono aduuwem Abasi!<verse eid="HEB 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 9:15" />Ke ntak ami, Krais ado akpe emem ke ufa edioomo nọ ato do mbon e-ekoodo ebọ nsi-nsi udeeme e-emaekenwọñọ, a-anye akpaaha nte andifak ammọ nsio ke mme ndiọiñkpọ e-ekenamma ke idak akpa edioomo.<verse eid="HEB 9:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 9:16" />Ke ñkpọ se ibaña ñwed edioomo adiaakpa, ana ewọt idiọọñọ ke andikinam ñwed ado ibaaha aba ke uwem, <verse eid="HEB 9:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 9:17" />sia esiben ñwed edioomo adiaakpa esịn ke adinam ke ini andikinam amaakekpa. Awo ikemeke adidat ñwed ado nsịn ke adinam ke ini andikiwed asʌkkọ ababa ke uwem. <verse eid="HEB 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 9:18" />Ami ado ntak a-awo i-imiikikamake akpa edioomo inam ñkpọ ndomokeed ibọhọke eduọk iyiib. <verse eid="HEB 9:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 9:19" />Ke ini Moses amaakekoot afịd ewʌhọ e-esịneke ke mbed anọ afịd awo, anye amaadat iyiib abaak enañ ye ake ebod, aben mmọọñ, ndad-ndad idededọñ ye ñkọk hisọb, asiime ke ñwed mbed ye afịd awo. <verse eid="HEB 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 9:20" />Anye amaabo, “Ami ado iyiib edioomo A-Abasi iwuuhọ ndufo abo enịm.” <verse eid="HEB 9:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 9:21" />Ke ukem usʌñ ado, anye amaasiime iyiib ado ke atayad ye afịd ñkpọ e-ekesikamake enam usọrọ. <verse eid="HEB 9:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 9:22" />Ke adinekke ntañ, mbed ayem naña ekpedat iyiib enam afịd ñkpọ asana, ndin mfeennọ ndomokeed ibaaha ke iyiib imiiduọkkọke.<verse eid="HEB 9:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 9:23" />Awuọ akena edat mme uwa ami enam mme mbid ñkpọ e-ebaññake ke hefịn esaana, ado akena ekama uwa a-afọnnọ akan enam ataa mme ñkpọ e-ebaññake ke hefịn esaana. <verse eid="HEB 9:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 9:24" />Sia Krais ikidʌkkọ itie ukpono e-ekedatta ubọk awo enam a-akedooho mbid ataa itie ado; anye akedʌk hefịn ke idem amọ, nọ ato do anye awuọ ada inọ ñnyịn ke iso Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 9:25" />Anye ikinyʌññọ idʌk hefịn adiwa idem amọ mmaana ñwaa, naña ekamba aku akesidʌk Nsana Mma Adisana Itie kwa isua ye iyiib i-imiikidooho ake amọ. <verse eid="HEB 9:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 9:26" />Akpedooho ntoro, awuọ Krais akpekena abọ ufen uwak-uwak ini tọọñọ ke ini e-ekebotto ederimbod. Ado idahami anye amaadi ini keed kpọd anọ afịd awo ke mme utịd ini ami adiben idiọọkñkpọ mfep ke anye adiwa idem amọ. <verse eid="HEB 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 9:27" />Kpa naña ana nte awo akpa akañ keed kpọd ndin amaama anye ada ikpe, <verse eid="HEB 9:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 9:28" />kpa ntoro ke ekewaa Krais inikeed kpọd nọ aben ndiọiñkpọ uwak awo afep. Ndin anye ayaamaana adi ayọhọ akañ iba, idooho adidibiom idiọọkñkpọ, ado adididat adinyaaña nsọk mbon e-etieghe ebet anye.<verse eid="HEB 9:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="HEB 10" />
  <para style="s1">Uwa Krais Ado Ini Keed Kpọd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 10:1" />Mbed ado ndukpọñ kpọd anọ mme nti ñkpọ se idi ke iso, idooho ataa mme ñkpọ ado ke idem ammọ. Ke ntak ami, ukem uwa e-ewaaha ke isua ke isua ikanna iyet mbon e-esañake ekpere adikpono Abasi nọ afọn ama. <verse eid="HEB 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 10:2" />Ekpekekanna, nte awo ikpikitreke adiwa ammọ? Sia ekpaekenam mme andikpono Abasi esana akañ keed kpọd, esịd ammọ ikpibiommo ammọ ikpe ibaña ndiọiñkpọ ammọ aba. <verse eid="HEB 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 10:3" />Ado mme uwa ado ekappa edo ñkpọ adidat ntoiyo ukwañ ñkpọ ke isua ke isua. <verse eid="HEB 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 10:4" />Iyiib ñyaara enañ ye ebod ikemekekeme adiyet mme idiọọkñkpọ mfep.<verse eid="HEB 10:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 10:5" />Ke ntak ami, Krais amaakedi ke ederimbod, anye amaabo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 10:5">“Uwa ye enọ, afo ukuyemme,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:5">ado afo amaatʌm itie ikpọkidem annọ miin;<verse eid="HEB 10:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 10:6" />esịd ikunemme fiin ibaña ufọfọb</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:6">uwa ye mme enọ uben mme ndiọiñkpọ mfep.<verse eid="HEB 10:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 10:7" />Ndin ami mmaabo, ‘Se ami mi, e-ewet ke ikpañwed embaña miin.’</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:7">Ami mmedi adinam uduak mfo, O Abasi mmi.”<verse eid="HEB 10:7" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 10:8" />Ke akpa ifed anye amaabo, “Afo ukuuyemme mme uwa ye mme enọ ye ufọfọb uwa ye mme enọ uben ndiọiñkpọ mfep, ammọ ikinyʌññọ unem fiin esịd” (akpesʌkado a-mbed akeyemme enam mme ñkpọ ado). <verse eid="HEB 10:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 10:9" />Ndin anye amaabo, “Se ami mi, ami mmedi adinam uduak mfo.” Ndin anye a-aben akpa uwa afep nọ ayọhọ iba asọọñọ ada. <verse eid="HEB 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 10:10" />Ato ke ntak uduak ado, e-enam ñnyịn isana ato ke adiwa ikpọkidem Yisọs Krais akañ keed kpọd.<verse eid="HEB 10:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 10:11" />Ke usen ke usen, aku keedekeed e-esida enam utom Abasi ammọ; enam emaana enam, ewa mme ukem uwa, a-adooho ikemekekeme iben mme ndiọiñkpọ mfep. <verse eid="HEB 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 10:12" />Ado ke Krais amaakewa uwa keed ke abaña mme ndiọiñkpọ, uwa a-akedooho nsi-nsi uwa, anye amaasuuk atie ke ubọk nnasia Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 10:13" />Tọọñọ ke ini ado anye asʌk abet tutu enam mme asua amọ ekappa edoñño ifịm udodukod amọ. <verse eid="HEB 10:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 10:14" />Sia amaato ke uwa keed anye anam mbon e-eyette esana efọn ema ke nsi-nsi.<verse eid="HEB 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 10:15" />Adisana Sịbidịd anyʌñ atie ntiense inọ ñnyịn abaña akpa edioomo. Ke akpa ifed anye ate:<verse eid="HEB 10:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 10:16" />“Ami ado edioomo se ami ndiinam ye ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:16">ke ini ado amaaboiyo, Abọọñ atañ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 10:16">Ami ñyaasịn mme mbed mmi ke esịd ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:16">ñyaanyʌñ ñwet ke akikere ammọ.”<verse eid="HEB 10:16" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 10:17" />Ndin anye adian do:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:17">“Ami ndiitoiyoke ndiọiñkpọ ye mme ubiad mbed ammọ aba.”<verse eid="HEB 10:17" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 10:18" />Ndin emaefeen afịd mme ñkpọ ami, ufọn uwa idiọọkñkpọ ibaaha aba.<verse eid="HEB 10:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ana Ekaka iso Eyịre ke Mbuọdidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 10:19" />Ke ntoro nditọeka ke Krais, sia ñnyịn imainie nsọọñọnda adidʌk ke Nsana Mma Adisana Itie ato ke iyiib Yisọs, <verse eid="HEB 10:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 10:20" />ato ke ufa usʌñ uwem e-ekʌkkọke eboiyo ke afọñ anyenusʌñ inọọ ñnyịn a-adooho abʌkidem amọ, <verse eid="HEB 10:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 10:21" />ndin sia ñnyịn iminie akwa aku a-akamake ufọk Abasi, <verse eid="HEB 10:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 10:22" />yak ñnyịn isaña ikpere Abasi ye esịd akpanikọ ke ayọhọ mbuọdidem, sia emaekekama mmọọñ a-asanake esiime ke esịd ñnyịn, enam ñnyịn isana inana ubiomikpe ke akikere ñnyịn, ñko sia emaekeyet ñnyịn idem nọ isana. <verse eid="HEB 10:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 10:23" />Yak ñnyịn isọñ ubọk imʌm idodanyen a-ñnyịn itañña anwa-anwa ibaña ikama, ikiidunyeeñe, sia anye a-akenamma enwọñọ ye ñnyịn ado anam akpanikọ. <verse eid="HEB 10:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 10:24" />Ñko, yak ñnyịn ikere naña ikpikan isọọñọ keed aken idem ke adiwọt ima ñnyʌñ nnam nti ñkpọ. <verse eid="HEB 10:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 10:25" />Yak ñnyịn ikiisịññe idem ikpọñ adisiboho itie keed, nte usʌk awo esinamma, ado yak isọọñọ idem, akpan-akpan nte ndufo ekịtte ke usen asʌk akpere.<verse eid="HEB 10:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 10:26" />Adieke ñnyịn ikoiyokoi ikaiso adinam idiọọkñkpọ ke imaikibọ ifiọk akpanikọ, uwa idiọọkñkpọ ibaaha aba, <verse eid="HEB 10:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 10:27" />ibọhọke adibeeñe idem ye ndịk mbet ubiideikpe ye ikañ iyadesịd a-adiita mme asua Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 10:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 10:28" />Awo ndomokeed a-akesịnne mbed Moses amaakpa ke unana mbọm ke emaekekop ito inua ntiense iba me ita. <verse eid="HEB 10:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="HEB 10:29" />Die ndin ke afo akere ke a-adot adikpimia awo a-asọnnọke Ayịn Abasi ke ukod ufen, awo a-adatta iyiib edioomo a-akenamma anye asana nte ndedeghe ñkpọ, a-anyʌññọ asọñ Sịbidịd mfọn anyen? <verse eid="HEB 10:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="HEB 10:30" />Sia ñnyịn imidiọọñọ andikibo: “Usiene annie miin: Ami ñyaasio usiene,” mfen ñko, “Abọọñ ayaakpe ikpe ikọd amọ.” <verse eid="HEB 10:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="HEB 10:31" />Ado ataa ekamba ñkpọ ndịk adiduọ ndʌk ke ubọk ndu-ndu Abasi.<verse eid="HEB 10:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="HEB 10:32" />Itoiyo akpa ini a-ndufo ekebọọhọ unwana, ini a-ndufo ekefiighe eda ke akpọsọñ ukuud. <verse eid="HEB 10:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="HEB 10:33" />Usʌk ini emaesinam ndufo ebọ usọñanyen ye ndutʌhọ anwa-anwa. Ke mme ini mfen ndufo emaeda keed ye mbon e-ekebọọhọ mme ukuud ami. <verse eid="HEB 10:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="HEB 10:34" />Ndufo emaekop mbọm enyʌñ ebọ ufen ye mbon e-esịneke ke ufọk ñkpakọb, ñko ke ini e-ekesikoonoke mme inie ndufo, ekesibọ ke inemesịd, sia emaediọọñọ ke ndufo emaenie mme inie e-efọọnọ ekan, e-ediinyʌñ ikpeene ke nsi-nsi. <verse eid="HEB 10:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="HEB 10:35" />Ke ntoro, ikiitop nsọọñọnda ndufo iduọọk, sia ndufo eyaebọ utịb ekamba-ekamba.<verse eid="HEB 10:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="HEB 10:36" />Ana ndufo esọọñọ eda esịn idem nọ ato do ke ini emaenam uduak Abasi, ndufo ebọ se anye akenwọñọ. <verse eid="HEB 10:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="HEB 10:37" />Sia,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 10:37">“Ke ataa etək-etək ini,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:37">anye a-anaaha adi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:37">ayaadi, idiikpeeneke.”<verse eid="HEB 10:37" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="HEB 10:38" />Ñko,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 10:38">“Ado adinen awo mmi adiidu uwem ke mbuọdidem.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 10:38">Ndin ami ñkoppo inemesịd ye anye a-atịmmeke edem.”<verse eid="HEB 10:38" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="HEB 10:39" />Ñnyịn isịneke ke atu mbon e-etịmmeke edem enyʌñ ebọ nsobo, ado isịne ke atu mbon e-enieghe mbuọdidem enyʌñ ebọ adinyaaña.<verse eid="HEB 10:39" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="HEB 11" />
  <para style="s1">Mbuọdidem Ado Anye</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 11:1" />Mbuọdidem ado nsọọñọnda ke se ñnyịn idot anyen ibaña, inyʌññọ inie eyighe ibaña se ñnyịn imiikịtte ke anyen. <verse eid="HEB 11:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 11:2" />Ami ado se eketooro mme ñkpisọñ esed ebaña.<verse eid="HEB 11:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 11:3" />Mbuọdidem anam inwaña ñnyịn ke ekebot ederimbod ato ewʌhọ Abasi; ke ntoro awo ikibotto mme ñkpọ se ñnyịn ikịt ito mme ñkpọ se ekekịt ke anyen.<verse eid="HEB 11:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 11:4" />Ke mbuọdidem Ebeel amaanọ Abasi uwa a-akefọnnọ akan ake Keen. Ke mbuọdidem emaetooro anye nte adisana awo, ke ini Abasi amaaketañ eti ikọ abaña mme enọ amọ. Ñko, ato ke mbuọdidem ke Ebeel aka iso atañ ikọ akpesʌkado a-anye amaakekpa.<verse eid="HEB 11:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 11:5" />Ke mbuọdidem emaeben Inọk esio ekpọñ uwem ami, ke ntoro anye ikikpaaha ñkpa. “Awo ikikịtte anye, sia Abasi amaaben anye asio.” Sia mbemiso ekeben anye esio, emaesọọñọ etooro anye nte awo a-akenemme Abasi esịd. <verse eid="HEB 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 11:6" />Ñko, awo i-imiinieghe mbuọdidem ikemekekeme adinem Abasi esịd, sia awo ndomokeed a-adiighe abịne anye ana anịm ke akpanikọ ke anye mmọdo, ñko ke anye ado andinọ mbon e-eyemme anye ke afịd esịd utịb.<verse eid="HEB 11:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 11:7" />Ke mbuọdidem, Nua, ke ini emaekewuuk anye ebaña mme ñkpọ a-anye imiikikịtte ke anyen, ke adisana mbaak, anye amaabọp ubom a-akenyaañake ufọk amọ. Ke mbuọdidem anye amaabiom ederimbod ikpe, amaanyʌñ akappa ado adiaakpa adinenido asañake ye mbuọdidem.<verse eid="HEB 11:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 11:8" />Ke mbuọdidem Ebraham, ke ini ekekoodo anye ebo aka itie a-anye adiikappa idat inie nte udeeme amọ, amaakop item anyʌñ akaa, akpesʌkado a-anye imiikidiọọñọke nte aka. <verse eid="HEB 11:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 11:9" />Ke mbuọdidem anye amaabọp ufọk ke isọñ enwọñọ nte asenawo ke asen idịd; anye akedʌñ ke atayad nana Aisik mme Yekọb ekedʌñ, e-ekedooho mme akpa adiaakpa ye anye ke ukem enwọñọ ado. <verse eid="HEB 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 11:10" />Sia anye akesʌk abek anyen anọ abio a-anieghe mme itiad idakisọñ, a-andikidomo ñnyʌñ mbọp adooho Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 11:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 11:11" />Akpesʌkado ini uman ayịn amaakeboiyo Sera, anye amaanie ukeme adiman nditọ sia anye amaadiọọñọ ke andikinam enwọñọ ado anam akpanikọ. <verse eid="HEB 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 11:12" />Ke ntoro amaato ke awo keed, a-aketieghe nte awo ñkpa, mme nditọ-nditọ emaemana e-ekewakka nte ntantaafiọñ ke ikpaanyọñ enyʌñ enana ibad nte ntan ke mben akpa mmọọñ.<verse eid="HEB 11:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 11:13" />Afịd ibon ami ekesʌk edu uwem ke mbuọdidem tutu ini a-ammọ ekekpaññake. Ammọ ikibọọhọ mme ñkpọ se ekenwọñọ, ado ekedaada ekịt mme ñkpọ ado ke anyan usʌñ, enyʌñ enyịmme ammọ. Ammọ emaenyʌñ enyịmme ke mmimọ idoñño mme adọdʌñ ye isenawo ke ederimbod. <verse eid="HEB 11:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 11:14" />Mbon e-etañña mme ñkpọ ntom e-ewọt ebo ke mmimọ isʌk iyeem abio a-adooho ake mmimọ. <verse eid="HEB 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 11:15" />Adieke ammọ ekpekekereke ebaña abio a-ammọ ekedakkake ekpọñ, ammọ ekpaekenie ufañ aditịmme ñkaa. <verse eid="HEB 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 11:16" />Utu ke ado, ammọ ekesʌk enie udọñ ebaña abio a-afọnnọ akan, a-abaaha ke hefịn. Ke ntoro, abuud inamma Abasi adikere Abasi ammọ, sia anye a-anam itie idʌñ anịm anọ ammọ.<verse eid="HEB 11:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 11:17" />Ke mbuọdidem Ebraham, ke ini Abasi akedomoke anye, amaayaak Aisik anọ nte ñkpọ uwa. Anye a-amaakebọ mme enwọñọ amaabeeñe idem adiwa ukweeñe ayịn amọ, <verse eid="HEB 11:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 11:18" />akpesʌkado A-Abasi amaakebo anye, “Adiito ke Aisik ke ubon mfo adiisakka.” <verse eid="HEB 11:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 11:19" />Ebraham amaadiọọñọ ke Abasi akeme adinam akpañkpa aset, ndin ke aditañ ke usʌñ mfen nte uwọdñkpọ, anye amaamaana abọ Aisik ye uwem asio ke ñkpa.<verse eid="HEB 11:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 11:20" />Ke mbuọdidem, Aisik amaadiọñ Yekọb ye Isọ ke abaña ini iso ammọ.<verse eid="HEB 11:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 11:21" />Ke mbuọdidem Yekọb, ke ini a-ñkpa ammọ akekeme, amaadiọñ nditọ Yosef keedekeed anyʌñ abere ke iwuod esañ amọ anọ Abasi ukpono.<verse eid="HEB 11:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 11:22" />Ke mbuọdidem Yosef ke ini amọ amaakekpere, amaatañ ikọ abaña nditọ Isrel adiwuọ ke ufʌn ñkpọñ Iyib, anyʌñ anọ uyio abaña naña ediibuuk akpọ amọ.<verse eid="HEB 11:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 11:23" />Ke mbuọdidem, ete ye eka Moses emaedịp anye afiọñ ita ke anye amaakemana, sia ammọ emaekịt ke anye ikidooho ñkaña nsekayịn, ammọ ikinyʌññọ ibaak ewʌhọ adidem.<verse eid="HEB 11:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 11:24" />Ke mbuọdidem, Moses, ke anye amaakekpon amaasịn adikere ayịn adiaha Fero. <verse eid="HEB 11:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 11:25" />Anye amaamek adikeene ubon Abasi mbọọ ufen utu ke adikop inem ke idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="HEB 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 11:26" />Anye akedat adibọ asuenne ke ntak Krais nte ñkpọ a-asọññọ udua akan mme nsọñudua inie isọñ Iyib, sia anye akewuuk anyen ase se idiido ñkpọ ayịnutom amọ ke ini iso. <verse eid="HEB 11:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 11:27" />Ke mbuọdidem, anye amaakpọñ Iyib, ikereke ibaña ifiobesịd adidem. Anye amaasịn ifịk, sia anye akesak iso ase anye a-awo imiikịtte ke anyen. <verse eid="HEB 11:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 11:28" />Ke mbuọdidem anye amaanịm Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo ye adisiime iyiib, nọ ato do andikiwoot akpa nditọ ideen adituuk akpa nditọ ideen Isrel.<verse eid="HEB 11:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="HEB 11:29" />Ke mbuọdidem mme awo emaesaña eboiyo ke ufọọd Ndad-Ndad Akpainyañ nte esaña ke nsaad isọñ, ado ke ini mbon Iyib ekedomoke adikeene nnam ntoro, ammọ emaedeñ.<verse eid="HEB 11:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="HEB 11:30" />Ke mbuọdidem mme ndibene Yeriko emaeduọññọ, ke ubon Abasi emaekesaña ke udịm ekanna usen itiaba.<verse eid="HEB 11:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="HEB 11:31" />Ke mbuọdidem, Rehab, awonwaan akpara, sia anye amaakefọn ido ye mbon uyeb, awo ikiwotto anye idian ye mbon i-imiikikoppo item.<verse eid="HEB 11:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="HEB 11:32" />Nsoo mfen ke ami ndiitañ? Ufañ ibaaha ami aditañ mbaña Kidiọn, Barak, Samsịn, Yefta, Defid, Samwel ye mme prọfed, <verse eid="HEB 11:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="HEB 11:33" />a-aketooho ke mbuọdidem ammọ enwana ekan mme abioubọọñ, ekpe unen ikpe enyʌñ ebọ se emaekenwọñọ; mbon e-ekekʌppọ mme ekpe inua, <verse eid="HEB 11:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="HEB 11:34" />eniime ifiobesịd mme edemeikañ; enyʌñ ebọkkọ akañkañ; mbon e-ekenamma mmemidem ammọ akappa adudu; e-ekekappake edoñño mme akop adudu ke ekọñ, enyʌñ esuan mme udịmekọñ mme asen idịd. <verse eid="HEB 11:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="HEB 11:35" />Ibaan emaemaana ebọi mbon ammọ e-emaekekpa esịn ke uwem. Mbon mfen emaaeba e-eketọtʌkkọke enyʌñ esịn adibọ ñkpọkñyak, nọ ato do ammọ enie adised ke ñkpa a-afọnnọ akan. <verse eid="HEB 11:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="HEB 11:36" />Usʌk ekebọ nsaha ye umia, ke ini ekebọppọ mbon mfen ke ñkpọnọ ukwak, enyʌñ esịn ammọ ke ufọk ñkpakọb. <verse eid="HEB 11:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="HEB 11:37" />Emaetọọñ usʌk ke itiad ewot. Ekeyọọyọọk usʌk ekpịkke iba, enyʌñ ewot usʌk ke akañkañ. Ammọ ekesiine ikpaedọñ ye ikpaebod nte afọñ, eba ke unana enyʌñ ebọ ndutʌhọ. <verse eid="HEB 11:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="HEB 11:38" />Ederimbod ikidotto adinie ammọ. Ammọ emaeyooñ ke mme akpautatan ye mme ikpọabod ye ke mme ukpe ye mme adu ke isọñ.<verse eid="HEB 11:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="HEB 11:39" />Emaetooro afịd mbon ami ebaña mme ntiense mbuọdidem ammọ, kpayeado ibaaha awo ammọ ndomokeed a-akebọọhọ se ekenwọñọ, <verse eid="HEB 11:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="HEB 11:40" />sia Abasi amaakeduak ñkpọ se ifọn ikan inọ ñnyịn, nọ ato ke adidiana ye ñnyịn enam ammọ afọn ama.<verse eid="HEB 11:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="HEB 12" />
  <para style="s1">Abasi Atʌnọ Nditọ Amọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 12:1" />Ke ntoro, sia utọ ekamba udịm mme ntiense ami ikannake ñnyịn ekʌk, yak ñnyịn itoomo afịd mme ñkpọ i-ibiọọñọke ñnyịn ye idiọọkñkpọ i-isịnne ñnyịn ukad iduọñọ. Yak isịn ifịk ifeghe itọk nduba e-ekenịmme inọọ ñnyịn. <verse eid="HEB 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 12:2" />Ñko, yak iwuuk anyen ñnyịn ke Yisọs, andido ntọọñọ ye andinam mbuọdidem ñnyịn afọn ama, a-akedooho ke ntak inemesịd e-ekenịmme ke iso amọ, anye akeyọ krọs, asọọn ndọk krọs, anyʌñ asuuk atie ke ubọk nnasia ke ebekpo Abasi. <verse eid="HEB 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 12:3" />Kere baña anye a-akeyọọhọ utọ mfiomo ado ke ubọk mme ndiọi awo, mbaak afo udukop mmemidem unyʌñ uduọ esịd.<verse eid="HEB 12:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 12:4" />Ke afo adinwana adibọkkọ idiọọkñkpọ, afo unwanake diin ukuwuọ itie adiduọk iyiib. <verse eid="HEB 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 12:5" />Nte ndufo emefre ikọ nsọọñọidem i-ikoodo ndufo nte ete akoot ayịn amọ? Anye abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 12:5">“Yịn mmi, kuudat ntʌnọ Abasi nte mfefeere ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 12:5">kuunyʌñ uyak esịd uduọ ke ini anye asuaha unọọ,<verse eid="HEB 12:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 12:6" />sia Abọọñ atʌnọ awo a-anye amaaha,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 12:6">anyʌñ asua anọ awo a-anye adatta nte ayịn.”<verse eid="HEB 12:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 12:7" />Iyọ nsọñọñkpọ nte ntʌnọ; Abasi ikama ndufo nte nditọ amọ. Sia akee nditọ ke ete imiitʌnọke? <verse eid="HEB 12:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 12:8" />Adieke ndufo imiibọọhọ ntʌnọ (ndin afịd awo e-ebọ ntʌnọ) awuọ ndufo idooho ataa nditọ. <verse eid="HEB 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 12:9" />Ñko, afịd ñnyịn imainie mme ete abʌkidem e-ekitʌnọke ñnyịn, ñnyịn ñko imaikpono ammọ ke ntak ado. Ke die ndin ke ñnyịn idiitre adisuuk idem nnọọ Ete mme sịbidịd, ñnyʌñ ndu uwem! <verse eid="HEB 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 12:10" />Mme ete ñnyịn emaitʌnọ ñnyịn ke etək-etək ini ke usʌñ a-ammọ ekekịtte ke afọn; ado Abasi itʌnọ ñnyịn ke ufọn ñnyịn, nọ ñnyịn ikeene iwuana ke nsana mma amọ. <verse eid="HEB 12:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 12:11" />Ntʌnọ ndomokeed inieghe inem ke ini afo abọọhọ anye, ado akama ubiak. Ado akem koo, anye adat idọk eti uwem ye emem asọk mbon e-emaekebọ ukpeeb ke anye.<verse eid="HEB 12:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 12:12" />Ke ntoro, inam ubọk ndufo a-akemeemme ye edọñ ndufo emaana esọọñ! <verse eid="HEB 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 12:13" />“Inam afañusʌñ ndufo ada ukem-ukem anọ ukod ndufo,” mbaak afekke ukod adikappa mbʌñọ, ado abọ nsọñidem.<verse eid="HEB 12:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndʌdutọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 12:14" />Inwana ke afịd usʌñ adiba ke emem ye afịd awo ye adinie adisana uwem, sia adisana uwem imiibaaha, awo ndomokeed idiikịtte Abọọñ. <verse eid="HEB 12:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 12:15" />Ikịt ibo ke awo ndomokeed itịppe mfọn Abasi, ñko ke idod-idod adʌñ ikọttọ isịn mfịna inyʌñ isappa uwak awo. <verse eid="HEB 12:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 12:16" />Ikịt ibo ke awo ndufo ndomokeed isịnne efịbe, inamma use, inyʌññọ inana Abasi nte Isọ, a-akedooho ke ntak usan ndidia keed anye akenyam unen udeeme amọ nte akpan. <verse eid="HEB 12:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 12:17" />Nte ndufo ediọọñọke, awo ikinọọhọ anye adidiọñ aba ini a-anye akediyemme, emaesịn anye. Akpesʌkado a-anye aketuaha ayem adidiọñ ado, ikikanna ikpəho se anye akenam.<verse eid="HEB 12:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Abod Ndịk ye Abod Idaara</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 12:18" />Ndufo idiighe ibịne abod e-ekemeke adituuk, a-anyʌññọ asak ikañ. Idiighe ibịne ekịm, ukuud ye ayobio; <verse eid="HEB 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 12:19" />me uyom adukpoñ me uyio a-atañña mme ikọ a-mme andikop ekpeiyekekpeiye ebo ke mmimọ iyemme adikop utọ ikọ ado aba. <verse eid="HEB 12:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 12:20" />Sia ammọ imiikikanna iyọ aba se ekenọọ ewʌhọ ebaña: “Akpedodo unam atuuk abod ado, ana etọọñ anye ke itiad ewot.” <verse eid="HEB 12:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 12:21" />Se ikitịppe amaanie ndịk tutu Moses abo, “Idem adiñnyenyek ye ndịk.”<verse eid="HEB 12:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 12:22" />Ado ndufo edi Abod Saiyọn, abio aduuwem Abasi, Yeruselem ake hefịn. Ndufo edi adikịt tọsịn mme tọsịn mme enyere ke mboho idaara, <verse eid="HEB 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 12:23" />ke ufọkabasi mme andikito mmana, e-emaekewet anyịñ ammọ ke hefịn. Ndufo edi ebịne Abasi, Abiideikpe afịd awo. Edi ebịne mme sịbidịd ndinen awo e-emaekenam efọọn ema; <verse eid="HEB 12:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 12:24" />edi ebịne Yisọs anditie ubiọñ ke ufa edioomo, enyʌñ edi ebịne adisiime iyiib a-atañña se ifọn ikan iyiib Ebeel.<verse eid="HEB 12:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 12:25" />Ikịt ibo ke ndufo isịnne atañikọ. Adieke ammọ imiikibọkkọke ke ini ekesịnne adikop uyio anye a-aketañña ikọ anọ ammọ mi ke ederimbod, die ndin ke ñnyịn idiibọkkọ, adieke ñnyịn ikannake iso ikpọñ anye a-atieghe ke hefịn idʌt ñnyịn utọñ? <verse eid="HEB 12:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 12:26" />Ke idahado uyio amọ amaanyeeñe isọñ, ado idahami anye a-anwọñọ abo, “Ke ini keed mfen ami ñyaamaana ñnyeeñe ederimbod, idooho ederimbod ikpọọñ, ñyaanyeeñe mme hefịn ñko.” <verse eid="HEB 12:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 12:27" />Mme ikọ ami, “ini keed mfen” ewọt adiben afịd ñkpọ se ekeme adinyeeñe mfep, a-adooho mme ñkpọ se ekebobot, nọ ato do ñkpọ se awo imiikanna inyeeñe asʌhọ.<verse eid="HEB 12:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 12:28" />Ke ntoro, sia ñnyịn ibọọhọ abioubọọñ a-ñkpọ ndomokeed imiidinyeeñeke, yak ñnyịn inọ ekọọm inyʌñ ikpono Abasi ke eti usʌñ, ke uteeñe ye ndịk, <verse eid="HEB 12:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="HEB 12:29" />sia “Abasi ñnyịn ado ikañ a-ataaha asobo.”<verse eid="HEB 12:29" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="HEB 13" />
  <para style="s1">Akpatre Ikọ Nnọitem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 13:1" />Ikaa iso idumakka emọ-emọ nte nditọeka ke Krais. <verse eid="HEB 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 13:2" />Ikiitre adikama isenawo, sia ke adinam ntoro mme awo emaekama mme enyere isen ke unana adidiọọñọ. <verse eid="HEB 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 13:3" />Itoiyo mbon e-ebaaha ke ufọk ñkpakọb nte akpedo ndufo ekeene ammọ eba ke ñkpakọb, ye mbon e-ebọọhọ ndutʌhọ nte ndufo ke idem ndufo ekpebaaha ke ukuud.<verse eid="HEB 13:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 13:4" />Akpena afịd awo ekpokpono ndọ, enyʌñ enịm ikʌk ndọ asana, sia Abasi ayaakpe ikpe ye mme asịn efịbe ye mme anam use. <verse eid="HEB 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 13:5" />Ikiiyak uwem ndufo ama akʌk, ado iyʌkkọ ke se ndufo enie, sia Abasi abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 13:5">“Tutu amama ami ndiikpọññọ ndufo;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 13:5">ami ndiiyʌññọ ifre ndufo ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="HEB 13:5" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 13:6" />Ado anam ñnyịn isọọñọ ida ibo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="HEB 13:6">“Abọọñ ado andiñnwam miin; ami ndiikoppo ndịk.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="HEB 13:6">Nsoo ke ñkaña awo akpekan annam miin?”<verse eid="HEB 13:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 13:7" />Itoiyo mme adaiwuod ndufo, e-eketañña ikọ Abasi inọọ ndufo. Ikere ibaña naña uwem ammọ aba inyʌñ idubọiyọ mbuọdidem ammọ. <verse eid="HEB 13:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 13:8" />Yisọs Krais ado ukem-ukem ñkpọñ, mfịn ye ke nsi-nsi.<verse eid="HEB 13:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 13:9" />Ikiiyak mme nsio-nsio isen ukpeebñkpọ enam ndufo edutịn usʌñ. Ado eti ñkpọ esịd ñnyịn adisọọñọnda ke mfọn, idooho ke adidia ndidia usọrọ, i-imiinieghe udod inọ mbon e-ediaha. <verse eid="HEB 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 13:10" />Ñnyịn iminie itie uwa a-mbon se inam utom ke atayad imiinieghe unen adidia ñkpọ ke esịd.<verse eid="HEB 13:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 13:11" />Ekamba aku asiben iyiib mme unam adʌk ke esịd Ataa Adisana Itie nte uwa idiọọkñkpọ, ado efọọmọ mme idem unam ke anwa esiin. <verse eid="HEB 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 13:12" />Ke ukem usʌñ ado Yisọs akebọ ndutʌhọ ke esiin inuaatob abio adinam mme awo esaana ato ke iyiib amọ. <verse eid="HEB 13:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 13:13" />Yak ñnyịn ndin ika ibịne anye ke esiin inuaatob abio; ibọ asuenne a-anye akebọọhọ. <verse eid="HEB 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 13:14" />Sia ke umi ñnyịn inieghe abio a-abaaha ke nsi-nsi, ado ñnyịn iyem abio a-adiidi.<verse eid="HEB 13:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 13:15" />Ato ke Yisọs ndin yak ñnyịn inọ Abasi uwa itooro afịd ini, mfịd ñkpọkinua a-akoodo anyịñ amọ inwañ-inwañ. <verse eid="HEB 13:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 13:16" />Ndin ikiifre adinam nti ñkpọ ñnyʌñ ñwuana se enie ye mbon mfen, sia utọ uwa ntoro asinem Abasi esịd.<verse eid="HEB 13:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 13:17" />Inie mbuọdidem ke idem mme etubom ndufo, inyʌñ isuuk iwuod inọ ukara ammọ sia ammọ ese ñkpọ ibaña ndufo nte mbon e-ediibọọrọ mbuume iwuod ndufo. Ikop item inọ ammọ nọ utom ammọ anọ ammọ inemesịd, idooho mbiomo, sia ñkpọ ntoro idiibaaha ufọn inọ ndufo.<verse eid="HEB 13:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 13:18" />Ibọñ akam inọ ñnyịn. Ñnyịn iminịm ibo ke esịd ñnyịn anwaña, ñko iminie udọñ adidu uwem a-anieghe ukpono ke afịd usʌñ. <verse eid="HEB 13:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 13:19" />Ami mmikpeiye ndufo akpan-akpan mbo ebọñ akam nọ emaana ensaana miin eyaak inọ ndufo usọp-usọp.<verse eid="HEB 13:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Edidiọñ ye Akpatre Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 13:20" />Yak Abasi emem, a-akemaanake aben Yisọs Krais a-amaakekpa adi ato ke iyiib nsi-nsi edioomo, ekamba Andikpeme mme edọñ ado, <verse eid="HEB 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 13:21" />ibana ndufo idem ye afịd nti ñkpọ nọ ndufo enam uduak amọ. Ñko yak anye anam ke idem ñnyịn ñkpọ a-anemme anye esịd, ato ke Yisọs Krais, a-anieghe ubọọñ ke nsi-nsi, nsi-nsi. Amen.<verse eid="HEB 13:21" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 13:22" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami mmikpeiye ndufo mbo yak ekpañ utọñ enọ ikọ nsọọñọidem mmi, sia ami iwet ndufo ibio-ibio ñwed kpọd.<verse eid="HEB 13:22" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 13:23" />Ami ñyem ndufo ediọọñọ ke e-esio ayịneka ñnyịn ke Krais, Timoti, ke ufọk ñkpakọb. Adieke anye asọppọ adisịm, ami ndiisaña ye anye ndikịt ndufo.<verse eid="HEB 13:23" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 13:24" />Kọọm afịd mme etubom ndufo ye mme afịd ndisana ikọd Abasi.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="HEB 13:24">Mbon e-etooho Itali enọ ekọọm isọk ndufo.<verse eid="HEB 13:24" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 13:25" />Mfọn Abasi aba ye afịd ndufo.<verse eid="HEB 13:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 13" />
</usx>